IDOR prevention in Spring Boot uses Spring Security's method-level security:

VULNERABLE CODE:
```java
@GetMapping("/projects/{id}")
public Project getProject(@PathVariable Long id) {
    return projectRepository.findById(id).orElseThrow();
}
```

SECURE APPROACH 1 - Use @PreAuthorize:
```java
@Service
public class ProjectSecurity {
    public boolean isOwner(Long projectId, String username) {
        Project project = projectRepository.findById(projectId).orElse(null);
        return project != null && project.getOwner().getUsername().equals(username);
    }
}

@RestController
public class ProjectController {
    @PreAuthorize("@projectSecurity.isOwner(#id, authentication.name)")
    @GetMapping("/projects/{id}")
    public Project getProject(@PathVariable Long id) {
        return projectRepository.findById(id).orElseThrow();
    }
}
```

SECURE APPROACH 2 - Filter in repository:
```java
public interface ProjectRepository extends JpaRepository<Project, Long> {
    Optional<Project> findByIdAndOwnerUsername(Long id, String username);
}

@RestController
public class ProjectController {
    @GetMapping("/projects/{id}")
    public Project getProject(@PathVariable Long id, @AuthenticationPrincipal UserDetails user) {
        return projectRepository
            .findByIdAndOwnerUsername(id, user.getUsername())
            .orElseThrow(() -> new ResponseStatusException(HttpStatus.NOT_FOUND));
    }
}
```

SECURE APPROACH 3 - Use Spring Security ACL:
```java
@Configuration
@EnableGlobalMethodSecurity(prePostEnabled = true)
public class SecurityConfig extends WebSecurityConfigurerAdapter {
    // Enables @PreAuthorize, @PostAuthorize annotations
}

// In controller
@PreAuthorize("hasPermission(#id, 'Project', 'READ')")
@GetMapping("/projects/{id}")
public Project getProject(@PathVariable Long id) {
    return projectRepository.findById(id).orElseThrow();
}
```

SECURE APPROACH 4 - Custom annotation:
```java
@Target(ElementType.METHOD)
@Retention(RetentionPolicy.RUNTIME)
@PreAuthorize("@authService.isOwner(#id, authentication.name)")
public @interface RequireOwnership {}

// Usage
@RequireOwnership
@GetMapping("/projects/{id}")
public Project getProject(@PathVariable Long id) {
    return projectRepository.findById(id).orElseThrow();
}
```

KEY PRACTICES:
1. Enable method-level security with @EnableGlobalMethodSecurity
2. Use @PreAuthorize for declarative authorization
3. Create repository methods that filter by owner
4. Implement custom authorization services
5. Use Spring Security ACL for complex scenarios
6. Always verify ownership server-side

IDOR prevention in Express.js uses middleware to verify ownership:

VULNERABLE CODE:
```javascript
app.get('/api/projects/:id', (req, res) => {
  Project.findById(req.params.id)
    .then(project => res.json(project));
});
```

SECURE APPROACH 1 - Custom middleware:
```javascript
const requireOwnership = async (req, res, next) => {
  try {
    const project = await Project.findById(req.params.id);

    if (!project) {
      return res.status(404).json({ error: 'Not found' });
    }

    if (project.ownerId.toString() !== req.user.id) {
      return res.status(403).json({ error: 'Not authorized' });
    }

    req.project = project; // Attach for next handlers
    next();
  } catch (err) {
    res.status(500).json({ error: 'Server error' });
  }
};

// Usage
app.get('/api/projects/:id', requireOwnership, (req, res) => {
  res.json(req.project);
});

app.put('/api/projects/:id', requireOwnership, async (req, res) => {
  req.project.name = req.body.name;
  await req.project.save();
  res.json(req.project);
});

app.delete('/api/projects/:id', requireOwnership, async (req, res) => {
  await req.project.remove();
  res.status(204).send();
});
```

SECURE APPROACH 2 - Use CASL for authorization:
```javascript
const { AbilityBuilder, Ability } = require('@casl/ability');

function defineAbilitiesFor(user) {
  const { can, rules } = new AbilityBuilder();

  // User can manage their own projects
  can('manage', 'Project', { ownerId: user.id });

  // Admin can manage all projects
  if (user.role === 'admin') {
    can('manage', 'Project');
  }

  return new Ability(rules);
}

// Middleware
const checkAbility = (action, subject) => {
  return (req, res, next) => {
    const ability = defineAbilitiesFor(req.user);

    if (ability.cannot(action, subject)) {
      return res.status(403).json({ error: 'Forbidden' });
    }

    next();
  };
};

// Usage
app.get('/api/projects/:id', async (req, res) => {
  const project = await Project.findById(req.params.id);

  const ability = defineAbilitiesFor(req.user);
  if (ability.cannot('read', project)) {
    return res.status(403).json({ error: 'Forbidden' });
  }

  res.json(project);
});
```

SECURE APPROACH 3 - Query filtering:
```javascript
app.get('/api/projects/:id', async (req, res) => {
  // Only find if current user owns it
  const project = await Project.findOne({
    _id: req.params.id,
    ownerId: req.user.id
  });

  if (!project) {
    return res.status(404).json({ error: 'Not found' });
  }

  res.json(project);
});
```

KEY PRACTICES:
1. Always verify ownership in middleware before controller
2. Use findOne with ownerId filter instead of findById
3. Implement reusable middleware for ownership checks
4. Use CASL or similar library for complex authorization
5. Return 403 for unauthorized, 404 for not found
6. Test with multiple user accounts
